            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 78-year-old female patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she displayed marked dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. She was promptly commenced on supplemental oxygen, nebulised bronchodilators, and a course of systemic corticosteroids. Continuous pulse oximetry monitoring was maintained throughout. Her respiratory status improved steadily, and she was discharged in a stable condition. I recommend continued follow-up for her COPD management and review of her inhaler technique and adherence. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
